    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4429" root="ثعب" body-key="v">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثَعْبٌ</span></b> , applied to water, (K,) and to blood,
(TA,) <i>Flowing, running,</i> or <i>streaming;</i> as also
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثَعَبٌ</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُثْعُوبٌ</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُثْعُبَانٌ</span></b> . (K, TA.) You
say ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَيْلٌ أُثْعُوبٌ</span></b>  [<i>A flowing torrent</i>]. (A.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
And [hence,] ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَرٌّ أُثْعُوبٌ</span></b>  (tropical:)  [<i>Evil that takes its
course like a stream</i>]. (A.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  See also what next
follows.

